Origin:
aicwf(4), a driver for the AICSemi AIC8800D80 FullMAC wireless adapter on
SDIO, the module of the Orange Pi Zero 4. It uploads the firmware through
the chip's boot ROM, brings it to a station interface and connects
net80211 to it the way bwfm(4) does: scan results, join, CCMP keys,
Ethernet frames both ways. The message formats and the order of
initialisation were read from the vendor's Linux driver; no code was taken
from it. The firmware file fmacfw_8800d80_u02.bin is not part of the tree
and is read from /libdata/firmware/if_aicwf.

Tested on the board: WPA2-PSK with CCMP on 2.4 and 5 GHz, DHCP, SSH and
eight rounds of 32 MiB each way with matching hashes at 10-17 Mbit/s. The driver announces 802.11a/b/g
only: with 802.11n the firmware leaves the reordering of aggregated
frames to the host. TKIP, WEP, power saving and access point mode are not
implemented.

--- sys/dev/sdmmc/files.sdmmc
+++ sys/dev/sdmmc/files.sdmmc
@@ -26,6 +26,11 @@ file	dev/sdmmc/sbt.c			sbt
 attach bwfm at sdmmc with bwfm_sdio
 file	dev/sdmmc/if_bwfm_sdio.c	bwfm_sdio
 
+# AICSemi AIC8800 FullMAC SDIO wireless adapter
+device aicwf: arp, ifnet, wlan, firmload
+attach aicwf at sdmmc
+file	dev/sdmmc/if_aicwf.c		aicwf
+
 # Broadcom SoftMAC SDIO wireless driver
 attach bwi at sdmmc with bwi_sdio
 file	dev/sdmmc/if_bwi_sdio.c		bwi_sdio
